   "source": [
    "### Section 1.2: Outlier Detection, Winsorization, and Scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Apply data quality transformations to prepare features for modeling.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Steps:**\n",
    "1. **Missing Value Analysis**: Identify columns with missing values after imputation\n",
    "2. **Outlier Detection**: Multi-method detection (IQR, Z-score, Isolation Forest)\n",
    "3. **Winsorization**: Cap extreme values while preserving price columns\n",
    "4. **Feature Scaling**: Robust scaling by sector (price columns protected)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Configuration Constants (code_guidelines.md Section 8.1):**\n",
    "- `IQR_MULTIPLIER`: 1.5 (for IQR-based outlier detection)\n",
    "- `ZSCORE_THRESHOLD`: 3.0 (for Z-score outlier detection)\n",
    "- `WINSORIZE_LOWER`: 0.01 (1st percentile)\n",
    "- `WINSORIZE_UPPER`: 0.99 (99th percentile)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Critical:** Price columns (`last_price`, `price_target`, `price_target_median`) are PROTECTED from winsorization and scaling per code_guidelines.md Section 8.5.2.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:**\n",
    "- Outlier detection summary\n",
    "- Winsorization effects report\n",
    "- `all_stocks_preprocessed` DataFrame ready for feature engineering"
   ],
   "id": "34b316f3eed03f42"
  },
